@startuml
!include style.iuml
mainframe class Abstract Factory
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Abstract Factory — as built (UML 2.5.1 class diagram)
interface DAOFactory <<interface>> <<abstract factory>> {
  +jobDao() : JobDAO
  +workerDao() : WorkerDAO
  +allocationDao() : AllocationDAO
  +auditDao() : AuditDAO
  +skillDao() : SkillDAO
  +userDao() : UserDAO
}
class OrmDAOFactory {
  +OrmDAOFactory(tx : TransactionManager)
}
class InMemoryDAOFactory <<unit tests>>
interface JobDAO <<interface>>
class OrmJobDAO
class "InMemoryDAOFactory.MemJobDAO" as MemJobDAO
class AllocationServiceImpl <<client>>
class BusinessTier <<factory>>
BusinessTier ..> AllocationServiceImpl : <<create>>\n(receives a DAOFactory)
AllocationServiceImpl --> DAOFactory
DAOFactory <|.. OrmDAOFactory
DAOFactory <|.. InMemoryDAOFactory
JobDAO <|.. OrmJobDAO
JobDAO <|.. MemJobDAO
OrmDAOFactory ..> OrmJobDAO : <<create>>
InMemoryDAOFactory ..> MemJobDAO : <<create>>
note bottom of DAOFactory
  One family per storage: relational (PostgreSQL or MySQL; the SqlDialect
  comes from DB_URL) or in memory (DB_URL=memory: and unit tests).
  The service never names a concrete DAO. See 28 for the Storage family above it.
end note
@enduml
